From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Annika Wickert <6527744+awlx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 11:36:23 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] gluon-mesh-batman-adv: emit raw throughput for Batman V
 neighbours

The Batman V neighbour list in respondd sent a pseudo TQ value. The
value came from the link throughput and was 255 for all links of
54 Mbit/s and more. Thus the map showed TQ 100% and no throughput.

Send the raw throughput in kbit/s in the "throughput" field instead.
yanic with Batman V support reads this field and writes source_tp and
target_tp to meshviewer.json.

Use json_object_new_int64() because the source value is uint32.

This is the gluon-parker port of the upstream change by Grische
(freifunk-gluon/gluon#3736). gluon-parker keeps the older Batman V
patch series, so the upstream patch does not apply.
---
 package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/src/respondd-neighbours.c | 5 +----
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/src/respondd-neighbours.c b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/src/respondd-neighbours.c
index 2950d1ec..0c0c9a64 100644
--- a/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/src/respondd-neighbours.c
+++ b/package/gluon-mesh-batman-adv/src/respondd-neighbours.c
@@ -59,7 +59,6 @@ static int parse_neigh_list_netlink_cb(struct nl_msg *msg, void *arg)
 	struct genlmsghdr *ghdr;
 	uint8_t *neigh;
 	uint32_t throughput;
-	uint8_t tq;
 	uint32_t hardif;
 	uint32_t lastseen;
 	char ifname_buf[IF_NAMESIZE], *ifname;
@@ -107,9 +106,7 @@ static int parse_neigh_list_netlink_cb(struct nl_msg *msg, void *arg)
 		json_object_object_add(opts->interfaces, ifname, interface);
 	}
 
-	tq = gluonutil_get_pseudo_tq(throughput);
-
-	json_object_object_add(obj, "tq", json_object_new_int(tq));
+	json_object_object_add(obj, "throughput", json_object_new_int64(throughput));
 	json_object_object_add(obj, "lastseen", json_object_new_double(lastseen / 1000.));
 	json_object_object_add(obj, "best", json_object_new_boolean(nla_get_flag(attrs[BATADV_ATTR_FLAG_BEST])));
 	json_object_object_add(interface, mac1, obj);
